A facile method of loading metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) onto cellulose aerogels (CA) to obtain hybrid aerogels for the removal of heavy metal ions in water. MOFs@CA composites can be easily separated; the equilibrium adsorption capacity of $\mathrm{Pb}^{2+}$ adsorbed by UiO-66-NH2@CA was $89.40~\mathrm{{mg}}$ $\mathbf{g}^{-1}$ The complete decomposition temperature $\mathrm{(T_{f})}$ of UiO-66-NH2@CA was increased by $62.1^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ compared with CA. The hybrid aerogels could be recycled without secondary pollution in the case of maintaining the adsorption performance.
