## 3.3 TG analyses
In order to determine the loading of UiO-66 and UiO-66-NH2 on CA, TG characterization was performed for UiO-66, UiO-66-NH2, and CA, and resultant UiO-66@CA and UiO-66- $\operatorname{\cdotNH}_{2}@$ CA composites to investigate the difference between the total weight loss temperatures as illustrated in Figure 4. In addition, the main thermal parameters are summarized in Table S2 (supporting information), including initial decomposition temperature $\left(\mathrm{T}_{0}\right)$ , maximum decomposition temperature $\mathrm{(T_{max})}$ and complete decomposition temperature $(\mathrm{T_{f}})$ .  The $\mathrm{{T_{0}}}$ , $\mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{max}}$ , and $\mathrm{T_{f}}$ of CA are $230.5^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , $332.2^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and $469.1^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , respectively. Compared with CA, the ${\mathrm{{T}}_{0}}$ , $\mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{max}}$ , and $\mathrm{T_{f}}$ of UiO- $66@$ CA are increased by $26.2~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , $20.7^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , and $60.7~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , respectively, and the T0, $\mathrm{T}_{\mathrm{max}}$ , and $\mathrm{T_{f}}$ of UiO-66-NH2@CA are increased by $26.7~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , $24.6~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , $62.1^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ respectively. Moreover, the CA aerogel showed lowest thermal stability than those of UiO-66@CA and UiO-66-NH2@CA composites, this could be due to MOF can be decomposed at higher temperature, which could improve the degradation temperature of UiO-66 $@$ CA and UiO-66-NH2@CA composites, providing higher thermal stability than CA aerogel. It has been reported in the published literature that after growth of ZIF-9 on CA, the T0, Tmax and Tf of CA are increased by $70.3~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , $30.6~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}.$ , $25.1^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ , respectively ( Ren, Gao & Lei, 2018). It can be conclude that the thermal stability results obtained in our work was in agreement with the previous study reported in the literature. Additionally, the weight loss of UiO-66@CA and $\mathrm{UiO-}66\mathrm{-}\mathrm{NH}_{2}@\mathrm{CA}$ composites UiO-66 were $8\mathrm{wt}\%$ and $6\%$ , respectively.
